<                             P1, P2 = genotype[0], genotype[2]
---
>                             # chrX outside the pseudoautosomal regions is haploid in
>                             # males, so the 1000 Genomes panel mixes "0"/"1" with
>                             # "0|1" in the same record. Indexing [2] unconditionally
>                             # raises IndexError on the first haploid call, after the
>                             # diploid records have already been written -- which
>                             # leaves a plausible-looking file holding PAR1 only.
>                             # Treat a single call as homozygous: haplotypes are
>                             # de-duplicated with set() below, so the duplicated
>                             # chromosome adds no weight, and keeping the count fixed
>                             # at 2 per genome is what the haplotype logic requires.
>                             P1 = genotype[0]
>                             P2 = genotype[2] if len(genotype) > 2 else genotype[0]
